<p class="inputs-lead">Rich form fields, each a tag of its own - a file of <code>pad/subs/inputs/types/</code>
in the engine, written <code>{pad:open/}input:name 'field'/{pad:close/}</code> or, when nothing else has the
name, bare. Every one posts a real value in a plain form submit, refills from the post and shows
the message of its <code>rules=</code>, as <code>{pad:open/}input:field{pad:close/}</code> does; its script makes
more of a native field where it runs. <a href="?form">One form</a> holds them all.</p>

<ul class="inputs-cards">
  {array:inputs}
  <li><a class="inputs-card" href="?{$kind}"><b>{$kind}</b><span>{$line}</span></a></li>
  {/array:inputs}
</ul>
